From: Florent Kermarrec <florent@enjoy-digital.fr>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv32: Prime the Gowin AE350 cache before LR/SC

A load and read barrier before each LR/SC attempt gives forward progress
on the Gowin AE350, including after eviction and across forked processes.
Keep the existing acquire/release ordering and retry semantics. Enable A
only around this sequence so that the rest of userspace can target RV32IM.

This patch is applied only by the Gowin AE350 Buildroot profile.

Signed-off-by: Florent Kermarrec <florent@enjoy-digital.fr>

--- a/arch/riscv32/atomic_arch.h
+++ b/arch/riscv32/atomic_arch.h
@@ -9,11 +9,16 @@
 {
 	int old, tmp;
 	__asm__ __volatile__ (
-		"\n1:	lr.w.aqrl %0, (%2)\n"
+		".option push\n"
+		".option arch,+a\n"
+		"\n1:\tlw %0, (%2)\n"
+		"\tfence r,rw\n"
+		"\tlr.w.aqrl %0, (%2)\n"
 		"	bne %0, %3, 1f\n"
 		"	sc.w.aqrl %1, %4, (%2)\n"
 		"	bnez %1, 1b\n"
-		"1:"
+		"1:\n"
+		".option pop\n"
 		: "=&r"(old), "=&r"(tmp)
 		: "r"(p), "r"((long)t), "r"((long)s)
 		: "memory");
